A||||5||8Ball||Met a couple local Fiero owners||||1||
Z||000000||8Ball||11-18-2001||06:41 PM||||Well in the last 3 days I have met 2 local Fiero owners. First one says he will be on here for certain. He owns a nearly mint (from what I could see) red 85 duke. Sweet ride!!! He is supposed to give me a ring soon also. He knows where a convertiable Fiero is in maryville for sale.<P>Second one was a young girl who bought an 88 maroon gt with coded ttops I was going to buy. Darn shame she bought it too. When I met her today she was on the side of the road awaiting the police. She just totaled that poor gt I loved so much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I am trying to buy it from her for parts for my car now.<P>Unfortunatly it is not repairable  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> She smashed the front pretty good. She pulled out into a major road and nailed another car in the side. Looks like she was going pretty fast as well. I really wanted that car too but the guy wanted 8 grand for it and I was not prepared to cough up that much dough. I offered her 500 for the car in the shape it is in now. Hope to hear from her soon. She seemed pretty interested in my offer considering the circumstances.<P>Anyway hope to hear from them both soon.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/8bff.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Master_Sushi||11-18-2001||11:05 PM||||To bad about that nice GT. All the fiero owners I have met have been nice people. I look forward to meeting more in the future!||||reg||14
